=== 与第一父比:defconfig 里 uart/console/baud 改动 ===
+# The panel stays a 4-line serial device: only CLK/CSN/IO0 are mapped to the
+# for D/C, which is exactly how the authority drives its serial panels on this
+# Memory Technology Device framework: the flash block's standard face
+# (mtd_dev_s) and its /dev/mtd0 node are in bk7258_flash_driver.c.
+CONFIG_MTD=y
+# Console baud, raised from the 115200 default.
+# Measured on the board: printing a `ps` table (~2 KB) over RPMsg -> CP -> UART0
+# at 115200 kept nsh_main at ~47% of the single AP core, so the shell felt
+# dead while the UI animated.  The console is a link-bandwidth problem, not CPU.
+# 1 MHz divides the 26 MHz XTAL exactly: 26000000/1000000 - 1 = 25, so the
+# programmed rate is exactly 1,000,000 (no rounding error, unlike 921600 whose
+# nearest divisor gives 928571, +0.76%).  UART_MAX_BAUD_RATE here is
+# UART_CLOCK/5 = 5.2 MHz, so 1 MHz is well inside the driver's own limit.
+CONFIG_BK7258_UART0_BAUD=1000000

